          "targetDoi": "10.1115/1.1420194",
          "snippet": "These transformations generally lead to a so-called inverse problem, where system properties and responses are known while excitations are unknown. It is well known that inverse problems are often 'ill-posed' in the mathematical sense, that is one of 1) the existence, 2) the uniqueness, or 3) the stability of solution is violated [2, 3,4,5]. If this inversion can be done, the system itself becomes its own force sensor.",
